{\b\fs24 Field Suite \endash  please read before installing}\par
Field Suite installs three offline applications for emergency response work: {\b Incident Report Manager}, {\b Field Toolkit} and {\b Field Map}.\par
{\b Support tools, not replacements.} Field Map supports, and does not replace, official CAD and dispatch systems. Map data, AED locations and event map files may be incomplete or out of date: confirm locations, road status and facility details with dispatch. The Field Toolkit first aid guide supports first aid training and does not replace it; its content must be reviewed by a qualified clinician before operational use. Follow your training, your organisation's protocols and the instructions of emergency dispatchers.\par
{\b Data on this computer.} Incident reports, drawings, messages and settings are stored on this computer and are not encrypted by the applications. Use device encryption (for example BitLocker) and keep backups. Uninstalling keeps this data.\par
{\b Amateur radio.} Field Map can show APRS stations without a licence. Sending your position or messages requires an amateur radio licence and your own call sign.\par
{\b Map data.} Map data \'a9 OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database Licence (ODbL). Other sources (Open Government Licence \endash  Canada, British Columbia, Alberta) are listed in Field Map under About & data sources.\par
{\b Third-party software.} The applications include the .NET runtime, SQLite, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite, SQLitePCLRaw and SkiaSharp under permissive licences (MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD, public domain). The full notices are installed in the Licenses folder.\par
